# The whole evidence tree, not one directory at a time.
#
# Every entry above this line names a single stage, which is how the tree came
# to hold 49 files in the native line ending of whichever machine published
# them: a directory nobody remembered to add was a directory whose bytes
# depended on the checkout. Evidence is compared byte-for-byte against what a
# verifier re-derives, so that difference is not cosmetic.
evidence/** text eol=lf

# Every file a published stage marker hashes, pinned to LF.
#
# A stage's source fingerprint answers "is the code in this tree the code that
# produced the published run?". Hashed over the checkout's raw bytes, it also
# answers "...as this machine happens to materialise text", so the same commit
# has one fingerprint under core.autocrlf=true and another on Linux, and a gate
# that was green where it was published goes red everywhere else. Pinning the
# hashed paths is what makes the question well-posed on every platform.
#
# Adding a path to a stage's _SOURCE_FILES means adding it here too. The
# contract test tests/contract/test_source_fingerprints_are_pinned.py enforces
# that, so a forgotten entry fails in CI rather than on somebody's laptop.
